The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) calls this one known issue with one fix queued. When you read
the reports themselves, they describe three problems. Two of them look the same from the desk, and
the queued parser fix closes only one.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Three tickets, three fixes. Fixing the parser leaves the other two open.
</Callout>

## What the reports say

<SplitTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first, so a day-first tenant's
  7 April comes out as 4 July. This hits every tenant on file and every channel.
- **`hint`**: the `booking-v3` form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, then reads the
  date day first. People type what the hint says. The symptom is the same, but the cause and the
  fix are different. Only form bookings at `booking-v3` tenants are affected.
- **`one-day`**: the date moves by exactly one day, and day and month are not swapped. "Client in
  Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday." This looks like a time zone bug. The desk
  had already noted these reports in `desk-notes.json`.

## Why they ended up in one ticket

- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line alone. All three
  problems arrive with the same subjects ("Wrong date again", "Month and day swapped?"), so the
  body was never read.
- Intake's tag is guessed from the reporter's browser, not looked up from the tenant. It is wrong
  in both directions, as the "intake tagged as" column shows. Count by tenant and form, as
  `causes.ts` does, and not by tag.
- The ticket export repeats some reports across its pages. Count each id once.

## The table on the incident page, for comparison

The incident page's own table (below) already finds `hint` but leaves it without a ticket. It
also files the one-day moves under `parser` with a footnote.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What to do with #4471

- Keep #4471 for the parser fix ([ticket](https://github.com/szymonczop/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1)).
- Move the `booking-v3` form reports to their own ticket ([ticket](https://github.com/szymonczop/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2)).
- Move the one-day moves to their own ticket ([ticket](https://github.com/szymonczop/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/3)).
  One reporter says they have stopped reporting these, so expect more than the export shows.
- Decision 0001 should be replaced by a new record (decisions are never edited) that merges on
  cause, not on subject.

